<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rochefort, Charente-Maritime</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rochefort is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charente">Charente</a> river in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, near the Atlantic coast. In 1666 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert">Colbert</a> chose the site for a new naval arsenal and dockyard, protected from attack by its position upriver, and it became one of the main bases of the French navy alongside Brest and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulon">Toulon</a>. Its seventeenth-century rope works, the Corderie Royale, still survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rochefort-charente-maritime.jpg" alt="Rochefort, Charente-Maritime" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CaptainHaddock · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_de_Rochefort.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
